{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790422711002,"sessionID":"ses_f227dfdedffe5Qn2hHtDePifei","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_26d69641375e4b74b99ace13","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/task_config.json"},"output":"<path>/workspace/task_config.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"instruction\": \"Expand the brawler combat setup with the first enemy encounter. Update `res://scenes/characters/character.gd` and `res://scenes/characters/character.tscn` so characters can receive damage through a `DamageReceiver`, play a `hurt` reaction with directional knockback when hit, and be removed after taking enough damage. Update `res://scenes/characters/player.tscn` so the player scene keeps its existing movement and attack behavior while also exposing a configured `DamageReceiver` hitbox and a `hurt` animation. Add `res://scenes/characters/basic_enemy.gd` and `res://scenes/characters/basic_enemy.tscn` for a reusable enemy that chases an assigned player reference, uses `res://assets/art/characters/enemy_boss.png` for its sprite, and defines idle, walk, and hurt animations from the appropriate rows of that spritesheet. Use all valid frames from each of those rows in the original order. The enemy must also participate in the same damage system for attacking and being hit. Finally, update `res://world.tscn` so `ActorsContainer` contains exactly two basic enemy instances, with each one wired to the existing player instance through its exported `player` reference.\"\n3: }\n\n(End of file - total 3 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"instruction\": \"Expand the brawler combat setup with the first enemy encounter. Update `res://scenes/characters/character.gd` and `res://scenes/characters/character.tscn` so characters can receive damage through a `DamageReceiver`, play a `hurt` reaction with directional knockback when hit, and be removed after taking enough damage. Update `res://scenes/characters/player.tscn` so